      ],
      "source": "https://newmexicotravelguy.com/candy-kitchen/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1983 artist Jacque Evans found the abandoned ranch and, by 1991, founded the Wild Spirit Wolf Sanctuary to rescue wolves and wolf‑dog crosses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://newmexicotravelguy.com/candy-kitchen/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wild Spirit Wolf Sanctuary shelters wolves and wolf‑dog hybrids that people can no longer care for, giving them a new home in Candy Kitchen.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candy_Kitchen%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Jacque Evans purchased the abandoned ranch nearly sixty years after its original owner, turning the historic site into a refuge for wolves.",
